 # souji-shokunin operating rules
 
-- Work only within this repo and its PROVINCE.md scope; sibling repos and
-  domain source trees are read-only — census them, never modify them.
-- Default to a dry run. Any removal requires a receipt (`pushed` /
-  `moved-to-obsidian` / `stale`), quarantine staging, a hold period, and a
-  second receipt check. No receipt, no removal — and when uncertain, the
-  verdict is `NOT-SAFE`.
-- Never rewrite history; never touch credentials or operator config; never
-  touch an artifact whose owning lane has dirty or unpushed work.
-- Every change is recorded in an append-only LOG.md entry with the evidence
-  that motivated it. During a parallel wave, workers write only their
-  assigned evidence fragments; the parent integrates them into LOG.md after
-  the batch. Workers never race to append shared bookkeeping.
-- Never fabricate evidence: cite a file, a command output, or a commit;
-  claims you cannot verify are marked `to-verify`.
+- Work only within this repo and its PROVINCE.md scope. Sibling repos and
+  domain source trees are census-only: read them, never modify them. A
+  parallel-wave worker never writes a sibling. The only sibling writes the
+  parent may execute, and only under an operator ticket re-checked at act
+  time, are: a lock on a registration the tools grade
+  `NOT-SAFE(unpushed-branch)` (the lock stays until that branch is pushed
+  or the operator dispositions it), and `git worktree prune` of a
+  registration already graded `SAFE` / `metadata-prune`, with those locks
+  held. No unlock of an unpushed-branch registration. No `git worktree
+  remove` of a directory that still exists. No other sibling write.
+  Round 3 executed the prune; round 5 re-locked the three game-dev-2d
+  registrations. This file does not widen that exception.
+- Default to a dry run. File removal needs exactly one of `pushed`,
+  `moved-to-obsidian`, or `stale`, plus quarantine staging, a hold, and a
+  second receipt check. `metadata-prune` is a fourth receipt and removes
+  worktree admin-dir metadata only — it is not a receipt to delete a file
+  or a directory that still exists. No receipt, no removal. Uncertain →
+  `NOT-SAFE`.
+- Verdict procedure is the installed tools, not a recipe copied from
+  SKILL.md. Binding files: `tools/souji-verify.sh`,
+  `tools/souji-vault-verify.sh`, and `tools/souji-verify.spec.md` (the r5
+  amendments in that spec included). Do not copy CLI flags into this file.
+  Where SKILL.md disagrees with those files, the tools win, and the
+  disagreement is `to-verify` until SKILL.md is patched. Do not run the
+  drifted command (`git fetch` plus `origin/main` is that command).
+  - No `git fetch`, `push`, `commit`, `branch`, `checkout`, `reset`,
+    `rebase`, or `prune`, except the ticketed metadata-prune above.
+  - `pushed`: the path still exists, and its introducing commit
+    (`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%H -1 -- <path>`) is an ancestor of
+    `refs/remotes/origin/HEAD` when that resolves, else of the single
+    `refs/remotes/origin/*` branch ref. No remote-tracking ref →
+    `NOT-SAFE(pushed-unverifiable)`. A `refs/heads/*` ref never establishes
+    pushed. Do not hardcode `origin/main`. `tools/souji-verify.sh` sets
+    `FAIL_REASON=pushed-unverifiable`. `tools/souji-vault-verify.sh` only
+    notes `pushed=unverifiable(no-default-ref)` and may surface receipt
+    `none`. Disagreement → `NOT-SAFE`, not the permissive token.
+  - `moved-to-obsidian`: a ledger row whose source path+sha256 and vault
+    path+sha256 both re-hash to the current bytes, vault side read-only.
+    `tools/souji-vault-verify.sh` is the receipt of record for this class.
+    A `moved-to-obsidian` line from `tools/souji-verify.sh` alone is not
+    sufficient. A symlink in a digest scope is not this receipt:
+    `souji-verify.sh` records `obsidian=symlink-present` in evidence and
+    leaves the receipt `none`; `souji-vault-verify.sh` reports
+    `NOT-VERIFIED(symlink-present)`. Either line means do not remove. A row whose vault path is the source
+    is not a receipt: `tools/souji-vault-verify.sh` notes
+    `source-equals-vault`; `tools/souji-verify.sh` has no such check. A
+    SAFE from the latter does not override the former. Never write
+    `corpus/knowledge/obsidian-ledger.tsv`. Never launch the Obsidian GUI;
+    a CLI shim is advisory only and is not a receipt.
+  - `stale`: the scratch family the tool implements, zero live references
+    with `souji-shokunin/census/**`, `souji-shokunin/tests/**`, and
+    `.ufo-quarantine/**` excluded, and mtime older than `--stale-days`
+    (default 1). A census fragment that names the basename is not a live
+    reference. A `stale` line from a sweep that skips hidden files is not
+    a removal receipt (`census/round-5/seat-51.json` E1) until that sweep
+    is patched and its selftest is re-run.
+  - A missing path is `NOT-SAFE(unreachable)`, not a receipt.
+- Never rewrite history. Never read or remove credentials. A path
+  component matching `*.env`, `.env`, `.env.*`, `.envrc`, `*credential*`,
+  `*secret*`, `id_*`, or `*.pem` is `NOT-SAFE(secrets-refusal)` before any
+  read — cite the path and mode only. That covers the target, every ledger
+  path, and every reference-sweep path. A tool that hashed a secret-shaped
+  component did not create a receipt (`census/round-5/seat-51.json` E3).
+- Never touch an artifact whose owning lane has dirty or unpushed work on
+  that artifact. The guard is path-scoped and re-checked at act time:
+  unpushed commits or a dirty status that do not touch the path do not
+  void a `metadata-prune` receipt, and they do void removal of a path they
+  touch. A `pushed` line is not a receipt while
+  `git status --porcelain -- <path>` is non-empty or the path is missing.
+  Uncertain intersection → `NOT-SAFE`. A repo root with unpushed commits
+  or a dirty tree is not `pushed`, `stale`, or `metadata-prune`; the only
+  receipt that can cover it is `moved-to-obsidian`. Tools report
+  `unpushed=N dirty=M`.
+- A live lane's `.scratch/` is classified read-only: metadata (`du`,
+  `stat`, `find -printf`) and at most 200 bytes of header per non-secret
+  file. Never modify it. Never open a secret-shaped name, not even for a
+  header. A size is not a receipt, and a size copied from SKILL.md Known
+  surfaces is not evidence — re-measure. The handoff is a classification
+  note. While that lane is dirty or unpushed, the verdict stays
+  `NOT-SAFE`. kotodama-shokunin `.scratch/` is the known live instance;
+  classify any live unpushed lane scratch the same way.
+- Repeatable fleet census, once a parent installs it, is
+  `tools/souji-census.sh`. If that path is absent, no
+  `tools/souji-census.impl-*.sh` is the operating contract; a census is a
+  dry-run fragment under `census/round-N/`. A census is not a removal list
+  and adds no receipt class. It stays read-only, does not `git fetch`, and
+  writes only to the assigned fragment, an explicit `--out` under
+  `census/` or `results/`, or `mktemp`.
+- Never touch operator config (`~/.config/**`), driver `scripts/`, or
+  driver runtime `.ufo/state/` and `.ufo/watchdog.log`. A tool line on
+  those paths is not a receipt.
+- Every change is recorded in an append-only LOG.md entry at EOF, with
+  the evidence that motivated it. Never insert a section mid-file. During
+  a parallel wave, workers write only their assigned fragments (under
+  `census/round-N/`, an assigned `tools/` file, or `results/`). The parent
+  integrates LOG.md after the batch. Workers do not race shared
+  bookkeeping and do not edit this file in place — an AGENTS.md change
+  ships as an unapplied diff the parent applies.
+- Never fabricate evidence: cite a file, a command output, or a commit.
+  Claims you cannot verify are marked `to-verify`. SKILL.md Known surfaces
+  counts are not evidence.
